Third-party material
====================

Fonts (app/src/main/res/font/chakra_petch_*.ttf)
  Chakra Petch, Copyright 2018 The Chakra Petch Project Authors
  (https://github.com/m4rc1e/Chakra-Petch), licensed under the SIL Open Font
  License 1.1. Full text: licenses/OFL-ChakraPetch.txt.

Muscle map shapes (app/src/main/kotlin/com/ironvellum/app/ui/program/BodyMapShapes.kt)
  Derived from react-native-body-highlighter (https://github.com/HichamELBSI/react-native-body-highlighter),
  main as fetched 2026-10-02, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 ELABBASSI Hicham. The muscle and head shapes and the
  hand-drawn outline (border) paths of its male and female bodies were converted by tools/bodymap_import.py.
  Full text: licenses/MIT-react-native-body-highlighter.txt, also shown in the app under Support, Licence.

Exercise drawings and instructions (app/src/main/assets/exercise_art/, domain/LibraryGuides.kt)
  Drawings adapted from two projects, both under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/; text in licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0-exercise-art.txt):
  - Everkinetic, created by Greg Priday (https://github.com/everkinetic/data), the exercise drawings and the
    instructions that the app's added movements are adapted from.
  - Workout Guide by Bryl Lim (https://github.com/bryllim/workout-guide, assets under CC BY-SA 4.0 via its
    LICENSE-ASSETS; its code is MIT). It expands the Everkinetic poses with more exercises and animation frames.
  Changes made: each frame was converted to a one-channel ink mask, cropped to the figure, scaled to at most 256 px,
  reduced to four ink levels and packed with its sibling frames into one WebP; the app paints the mask in its own
  ink colour at draw time. Some faint frames were brightened. The drawings and the instruction text adapted from them
  stay under CC BY-SA 4.0; the rest of the app is GPL-3.0-or-later. Details and the per-drawing record:
  docs/ART_ATTRIBUTION.md and tools/exercise_art/.

Artwork
=======

Apart from the exercise drawings credited above, all artwork is original to Ironvellum. Rank emblems are hand-authored vectors;
the launcher icon, empty-state and crest images were generated for this
project with Google Gemini (tools/art.py). All of it is released under the
project licence above. Details: docs/ART_ATTRIBUTION.md.
